## 14. Communication Discipline

**Rule:** Agents communicate progress, blockers, and decisions clearly.

**In PR Body:**
- Summary of changes (what and why)
- Architecture compliance statement (which docs followed)
- Testing performed (QA D checklist results)
- Known limitations or follow-up tasks
- Deployment notes (env vars, migrations, etc.)

**When Blocked:**
- Document blocker with context
- Suggest resolution options
- Escalate to BLD Bot if Architecture conflict
- Do NOT proceed with conflicting code

**Example PR Body:**
```markdown
## Summary
Implements LSS Shepherding schedule automation per Event Standards v1.

## Architecture Compliance
- Follows Event Standards v1 § LSS section
- Uses Asia/Manila timezone per § Principles
- Enforces first Sat–Sun of March (Feb flex) per § LSS cadences

## Testing (QA D)
- [x] Lint clean
- [x] TypeScript compiles
- [x] Unit tests pass (12 new tests)
- [x] Manual testing: created LSS series, verified 6 Tue sessions generated
- [x] Security: N/A (no auth/member data changes)

## Deployment Notes
- No new env vars
- No migrations (uses existing `events` table)

## Known Limitations
- LSS Team report deferred (out of v1 scope per Event Standards)
```

